<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boril of Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1207–<a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Tsar Boril</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boril was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1207 to 1218, a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaloyan-of-bulgaria">Kaloyan</a>, whose throne he took after Kaloyan's death. He fought the Latin Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and rebel relatives such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexius-slav">Alexius Slav</a>, and in 1211 he called a church council against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogomil">Bogomil</a> heresy. He was overthrown by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-asen-ii">Ivan Asen II</a> and blinded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boril-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Boril of Bulgaria" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Boril.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
